um_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Stages (Section 6(c)/12(d)(1)/17(b) exemptive relief):**\n\n1. **Application:** File on EDGAR under Rule 0-2. Staff comments, and amendments follow. Standard review has no fixed deadline; Rule 0-5 gives staff a target to comment, not a guarantee.\n2. **Notice:** Once staff is satisfied, the SEC issues a notice (Federal Register/release) with a hearing-request deadline, typically about 25 days.\n3. **Order:** If no hearing is requested, staff usually grants the order under delegated authority. If a hearing is requested, the SEC may hold one or decide the matter itself.\n\n**Rule 0-5(d) expedited review:** Available when the application is substantially identical to two precedent applications granted within the prior two years. The filing needs a marked comparison and a certification. Novel terms are ineligible.\n\n**The 45-day clock:** Notice is targeted within 45 days of filing. Staff can extend this, toll it for amendments, or move the application to standard review. It measures time to **notice**, not to the final order.","ttft_ms":6487,"type":"result","duration_ms":9879,"uuid":"2c80610d-964f-4996-b24e-e5846c45e3fb","ttft_stream_ms":1138,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":1139,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
